# PIN locations are locked

Do **not** change pin lat/lng, pin order, or relocate pins on the map unless the user explicitly asks to move a specific pin.

- Softening GPS/audio gates is OK
- Swapping or snapping pin coordinates is **not** OK without asking
- If a pin location was changed by mistake, restore it immediately
- Never move unrelated pins while editing audio/GPS logic
- Route 2 pins 10–11 stay as currently set (correct)

